151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,2629,315,279,1378,2750,892,686,1281,279,2701,7493,5614,30,26107,59,37018,45340,12,18,15170,17,87,61,17,12,23,87,10,22,92,14085,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the sum of the two values which will make the following expression undefined? $$\\frac{x-3}{2x^2-8x+7}$$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"41b4ec635557a41207a67e3e5a955ea0e61637afff2203e36b333d6a123bf7e0"},"seconds":14.956593751907349,"seed":766364540305932689,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the values of \\( x \\) that make the expression \\(\\frac{x-3}{2x^2-8x+7}\\) undefined, we need to identify the values of \\( x \\) that make the denominator zero. The expression is undefined when the denominator is zero because division by zero is not defined.\n\nLet's start by setting the denominator equal to zero and solving for \\( x \\):\n\\[\n2x^2 - 8x + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation. To solve it, we can use the quadratic formula, which is given by:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n\\]\nwhere \\( a = 2 \\), \\( b = -8 \\), and \\( c = 7 \\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the discriminant (\\( \\Delta \\)):\n\\[\n\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac = (-8)^2 - 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 7 = 64 - 56 = 8\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( \\Delta \\) into the quadratic formula:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-(-8) \\pm \\sqrt{8}}{2 \\cdot 2} = \\frac{8 \\pm \\sqrt{8}}{4}\n\\]\n\nSimplify \\( \\sqrt{8} \\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{8} = \\sqrt{4 \\cdot 2} = 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( 2\\sqrt{2} \\) back into the formula:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{8 \\pm 2\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression by dividing both terms in the numerator by 4:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{8}{4} \\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{4} = 2 \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the two values of \\( x \\) that make the denominator zero are:\n\\[\nx_1 = 2 + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x_2 = 2 - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\]\n\nTo find the sum of these two values, we add them together:\n\\[\nx_1 + x_2 = \\left(2 + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) + \\left(2 - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\nCombine the terms:\n\\[\nx_1 + x_2 = 2 + 2 = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the two values which make the expression undefined is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{4}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:1006"}
